  "configuration_id": "config_039",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_038 (multimodal, multiprofile, scVI_n200, ViT_L, transformer, concat) achieved the best validation accuracy (0.721) so far, a ~7-point gain over the best RNA-only config (0.653). However, we have no evidence about whether the concat fusion is optimal or whether the two modalities have asymmetric information content that a weighted fusion could exploit. Question: config_039 is identical to config_038 except fusion changes from concat to weighted, isolating the effect of fusion strategy. This tells us whether the modalities contribute equally (concat sufficient) or unequally (weighted better), which is a fundamental design decision for all future multimodal experiments. Why this is the best next experiment: it is a minimal single-variable change from the current best configuration, directly comparable to config_038, and resolves an important uncertainty about how to combine modalities before investing further experiments in other design axes (aggregation, image encoder choice, or RNA encoder). Under a limited budget, this clean A/B comparison maximizes information per experiment."
}

